# Frontend architecture — PokeSlider

## Entry & shell

- `main.tsx` → `AppProviders` → `App`.
- Global styles: `index.css` imports Tailwind + `styles/design-tokens.css`.
- Keyboard shortcuts: `hooks/useAppKeyboardShortcuts.ts` (document-level; respects inputs / `defaultPrevented`). **Escape order:** team builder modal → compare modal → My Dex panel → details overlay.

## Feature boundaries

| Feature | Primary files |
|---------|----------------|
| Carousel | `features/carousel/PokeBallCarousel.tsx`, `hooks/usePokeBallCarousel.ts` |
| Ball/Pokémon overlay | `features/overlay/DetailsOverlay.tsx`, `BallDetailPanel.tsx`, `PokemonDetailPanel.tsx` |
| My Dex | `features/discovery/MyDexPanel.tsx`, `discoveryEngine.ts`, `useMyDexDiscovery.ts`, `discoveryUiStore.ts` |
| Compare | `features/compare/*`, `store/comparisonStore.ts` |
| Team Builder | `features/team-builder/*` (modal, `teamBuilderEngine.ts`, `useTeamBuilderData.ts`, `typeMatchupChart.ts`), `store/teamBuilderStore.ts`, `services/pokeapi/typeMatchupChart.ts` |
| Atmosphere | `providers/AppAtmosphere.tsx` (reads species types into `html[data-atmosphere]`) |

## Composition rules

- **App** orchestrates layout + skip link + `main`; it should not accumulate business logic.
- **Overlays** own their focus trap container ref; do not mount a second QueryClient per modal.
- **Discovery** keeps list virtualization optional — current list is client-filtered; if virtualizing, isolate in a sub-component.

## Providers

- `AppProviders`: single `QueryClient` instance (stable via `useState` initializer).
- Do not add Context providers unless more than one consumer needs the same mutable instance without Zustand.

## Assets & public

- Poké Ball and Pokémon images are remote URLs (PokéAPI / GitHub sprites). No local sprite pipeline in repo.

## Anti-patterns here

- Fetching inside Zustand actions — use Query + `queryClient.fetchQuery` / `prefetch` instead.
- Putting PokéAPI response types in components — import from `types/` or feature-local types.
